    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Embraced in Italy in the mid-1700s, Karen Chartry spent two centuries allying herself with the Ventrue of one city after another before settling in New Orleans in the 1940s. She has since built herself into one of the city's most influential Kindred by courting the intelligentsia &mdash; a constituency Marcel largely ignores &mdash; and has become the de facto (if unelected) leader of the Prince's Council, which frequently meets and acts without informing Marcel, though rarely without informing Karen. Her one notable misstep came when she became infatuated with the art student Josua Cambridge and, failing to seduce him away from his obsessive painting, arranged to have her own childe, Julia Cammeron, ruin him &mdash; a scheme that instead resulted in Julia Embracing Josua and delivering him into Marcel's household. Karen has since quietly spread the rumor that one of Morgaine's associates was responsible, and continues visiting Josua under the guise of concern.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Coolly aloof even with your own clan &mdash; every kindness you extend is a debt collected later.</p><p><strong>Disciplines (as printed, dot-rating, converted to owned Discipline Items on this Actor at Storyteller discretion):</strong> Auspex 2, Celerity 4, Dominate 5, Fortitude 4, Obfuscate 1, Potence 2, Presence 4, Protean 3, Quietus 2, Thaumaturgy 2 (Lure of Flames 2).</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Contillio. Feeds only on men with demonstrated artistic talent. Effective leader of the Prince's Council, though not an official member; her rival for influence is Morgaine, who is also not a Council member. Haven: a three-story home in the Garden District. Secrets rating: A-.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
